 "description": "FRUSTRATION as the PSI REGRESS-BREAKER (block 226000): futile repetition -- repetition WITHOUT understanding-gain -- raises a leaky scale2-decayed frustration modulator that, past a threshold, BREAKS the loop (STOP). Frustration is the emotional COMPLEMENT to the 221000 understanding drive (understanding rewards compression; frustration punishes futile repetition). THE DISCRIMINATOR: a step is FUTILE iff it RECURS (an Exists MATCH over the has_step history) AND yields no gain (d_hyp==0 AND d_state==0 AND s_drop==0 -- the raw observables the adapter stamps, the 208000 ev_* pattern); a PRODUCTIVE repeat is NOT marked futile so frustration stays flat -- NOT a repeat-counter. fr_mark_futile marks it; fr_accumulate is the 215000 gs_grievance_from_slights leaky Sum(Times(futile, Ashr(unit, age/half_life))); fr_break reads the modulator across the threshold and sets break_now=STOP. Integer-native, NO Rust, NO new Term. self_load_only + depends_on [] + every rule guarded on HeldFrustrationParams.enabled==1: default-OFF and byte-identical when absent.",
 "microtheory": {
  "name": "ls20_frustration",
  "description": "Frustration is a leaky accumulator of FUTILE-repeat events (recurrence with no understanding-gain); crossing a threshold it breaks the current strategy (stop/switch). It is the emotional regress-breaker -- the complement of curiosity: the same understanding signal that rewards compression, read with the opposite sign on futile repetition."
